{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/RepJamesClyburn/posts/trumps-concept-of-a-plan-is-to-give-money-directly-to-americans-for-health-carew/1370696621089039/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/RepJamesClyburn/posts/trumps-concept-of-a-plan-is-to-give-money-directly-to-americans-for-health-carew/1370696621089039/","title":"James E. Clyburn","description":"Trump’s “concept of a plan\" is to give money directly to Americans for health care—without the ACA protections that have enabled more than 20 million Americans to afford high-quality insurance.\n\nThe...","language":"en","text":"Trump’s “concept of a plan\" is to give money directly to Americans for health care—without the ACA protections that have enabled more than 20 million Americans to afford high-quality insurance.\n\nThe likely result would be increased costs for those most in need of care.\n\nAll reactions:\n\n170 comments\n\n26 shares\n\nLike\n\nComment\n\nMost relevant\n\n\n\nDeeDee Henderson\n\nThis sounds great, except that anyone who understands healthcare understands that the power of negotiation in healthcare does not come from 1 person, but from groups. A group of 30 million people can demand much more than 1 person alone. Congress literally is supposed to represent every American citizen and should be able to negotiate a universal healthcare plan for all citizens.\n\n5\n\nMary Ann\n\nDoes this make sense to anyone?\n\n8\n\nView all 5 replies\n\nPatricia McElroy\n\nI’m sure insurance companies will be jumping at the chance to negotiate with us, as individuals.\n\n16\n\nView 1 reply\n\nShaun Ritchie\n\nHow far will 2k go? About 3-6 months just for premiums not including co pays and prescriptions…\n\n5\n\nDonna Cochran\n\nI guess he means for us to negotiate with insurance companies like we do for home, auto. We’re definitely winning that fight.\n\n3\n\nView all 2 replies\n\nDeborah Kauffman Kuhling\n\nAnd just how does this lower the cost of insurance?\n\n2\n\nView all 2 replies\n\nBarbara Bushey Ernico\n\nTrump really doesn’t understand healthcare needs or insurance. I find it ironic that he grouses about insurance companies being trillionaires but doesn’t bat an eye about others’ unscrupulous methods of becoming trillionaires.\n\nI pray to God daily!\n\n1\n\nKeith Ford\n\nAnd how much will premiums go up? Hmm, let me think.\n\n5\n\nView all 6 replies\n\nKelvin Tolbert\n\nHow about putting in the Public Option for the people to choose from. Have the insurance company compete against a program similar to Medicare that the people can choose to buy into rather than an insurance policy.\n\n2\n\nView all 4 replies","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":5442.879826994613,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}